  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multipurpose cash transfers to Chadian returnees and host communities in the province of Wadi FiraMultipurpose cash transfers to Chadian returnees and host communities in the province of Wadi Fira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of 2025, Wadi Fira province in eastern Chad has seen a sharp increase in the number of Chadian returnees, primarily fleeing the escalating conflict in North Darfur (Sudan), including violence near Zam Zam camp and Al Fasher. To address urgent needs, IOM is providing multi-purpose cash assistance (MPCA) to returnee and host community households. The intervention aims to alleviate immediate hardship, support self-reliance, and reduce pressure on overwhelmed host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
